graphify-out/

# Claude Code: live session lock, not project config
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# ─── Real BVD data — local only, never committed ──────────────────────────
# Git history is permanent and repo visibility is one misclick, so neither of
# these is ever committed, private repo or not. Each has small synthetic
# stand-ins that ARE committed and are what CI runs; the real files are read
# only by describe.skipIf blocks that skip automatically when they are absent
# (see parseInvoiceCsv.test.ts and parseBvdCsv.test.ts).
#
# data/bvd-invoices/ — real per-driver, per-transaction financial data (who
# bought how much fuel, where, when, for how much). Synthetic fixtures live in
# backend/test/fixtures/invoices/.
data/bvd-invoices/
# data/bvd-prices/ — BVD's daily price sheets: contract pricing. Untracked in T-51;
# earlier commits still contain them (see T-50 for the history decision).
# Synthetic fixtures live in backend/test/fixtures/bvd-prices/.
data/bvd-prices/

# docs/design/*.dc.html — exported design mockups embed a real slice of the
# 999210 invoice (real gallons/billed prices across 16+ rows) as inline JS
# mock data, not just the handful of figures documented in PROJECT-SCOPE-v2.md
# §A19. Untracked in T-58; earlier commits still contain it (see T-50/T-58 for
# the history decision).
docs/design/*.dc.html

# migrations/real/ — the real fleet roster (real driver names, real BVD
# fuel-card numbers), mirroring migrations/synthetic/ file for file (T-58).
# migrations/synthetic/ is what a fresh clone, CI and `db:migrate` apply by
# default; point runMigrations at migrations/real instead, locally, to test
# against the real invoice. Never committed, same reasoning as the rows above.
migrations/real/
